WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.602
-Hello, everyone,
and welcome back.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.503
This is our second to last show
in the captain's quarters,

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:06.972
and we're starting to worry
we're just not gonna get to

00:00:06.972 --> 00:00:08.541
everything we wanted to get to.

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:11.110
For example, I wanted to do
a whole new book bit

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.780
where I would take a book
and replace the "bird"

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.348
in the title with "Thorn Birds."

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:17.149
For example,
"To Kill a Mockingbird"

00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:19.652
would appear behind me and
then later would mysteriously

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.554
change to
"To Kill a Thorn Bird."

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.055
I think that would have
been amazing,

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:24.691
but we didn't have time.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:27.460
I also hoped that, by not
cutting my hair for six months,

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.562
it would magically transform
into Steff hair

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.931
from "Pretty in Pink,"
but instead it seems to be

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:34.968
trending towards
summertime Steve Bannon.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:37.971
You know, "Point Broke"
over there.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.605
"Utah, gimme ten!"

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:42.241
But one thing we did promise you
was a B-plot

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:45.344
wherein the Sea Captain
faces off with his nemesis,

00:00:45.344 --> 00:00:47.013
a giant ghost lobster.

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:49.849
And since we have never
broken a promise to you,

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:54.754
here it is, for your enjoyment,
that exciting action sequence.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:57.323
-The time for reckoning
is now!

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.192
-Release me, foul beast!

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:01.461
-20 seconds until he drags you

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:04.597
into a watery grave,
Sea Captain!

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:07.099
-Quick, Ira, throw me
that spoon.

00:01:07.099 --> 00:01:08.634
-Right away, Sea Captain.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:11.437
-Steve, give me that weird egg
with the lighthouse on it.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.206
-You got it, Sea Captain.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.541
-Vickie, toss me
that wooden buoy.

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:17.443
-The mermaid's name is Vickie?

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:19.244
-We never established it wasn't.

00:01:19.244 --> 00:01:21.447
Oh, hey, that reminds me
of a joke.

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:23.349
-We don't have time for this,
Sea Captain.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.818
-Well, maybe if your stupid
"Closer Looks" weren't so long,

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:27.753
we would have time for it.

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:29.021
-Maybe they wouldn't be so long

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:30.322
if you didn't interrupt
so often.

00:01:30.322 --> 00:01:32.058
-Ten seconds, Sea Captain!

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.926
-Do you want to hear
the joke or not?

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:35.661
-Fine.
-Okay.

00:01:35.661 --> 00:01:38.064
What do you call
a mythical creature

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.765
at her best friend's wedding?

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:41.233
-Is it a mermaid of honor?

00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:43.436
-No!

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.705
Okay, yes, it --
it actually --

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.006
You got it.

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.575
-♪ Sea Captain! ♪

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:51.377
-Watch "MacGruber" on Peacock.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:52.712
-Sometime next year.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.180
-And speaking of explosions --

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.049
-Segue plug!
-The President --

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:58.417
-Oh, hey, Seth, if we're
plugging stuff,

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:00.753
I have a new podcast.
It's called "Duck and Cover."

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.021
Because, you know, I'm a duck

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:03.989
and it covers my take
on world events.

00:02:03.989 --> 00:02:05.825
You know, just my musings
and whatnot.

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.226
-You're really throwing
the brakes

00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:08.727
on the momentum here, Ira.

00:02:08.727 --> 00:02:10.963
-Okay, so I can't plug
my projects.

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:13.065
Okay, that's really helpful
to know. Thank you.

00:02:13.065 --> 00:02:15.568
-What can I say?
I'm gonna miss these guys.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:18.404
The President and Fox News are
desperately trying to distract

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.306
from the Democratic National
Convention.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:23.175
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:02:23.175 --> 00:02:27.112
♪♪

00:02:27.112 --> 00:02:29.882
Donald Trump has been trying to
counter-program the DNC

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:31.283
with his own campaign events.

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:33.786
And look, whatever you want
to say about Trump --

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:35.488
like he's an incompetent,
grifting,

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.389
sociopathic golf ogre --

00:02:37.389 --> 00:02:40.059
at least he's also
a terrible campaigner.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.728
He's been trying to win over
voters he condescendingly

00:02:42.728 --> 00:02:45.031
refers to as
"suburban housewives,"

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.833
with some bald-faced
racism,

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:49.235
and in Wisconsin on Monday,
he took another shot

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:53.172
at wooing that key voting bloc
by continuing to insult them.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:56.676
-But this is the future that
Joe Biden plans to bring

00:02:56.676 --> 00:03:00.546
to every city, town,
and suburb in our nation.

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:02.415
And, you know,
for those suburbs,

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:05.851
I keep hearing about
suburban women.

00:03:05.851 --> 00:03:08.921
I made the --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:09.922
Oh.

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:12.691
[ Cheering continues ]

00:03:12.691 --> 00:03:16.896
Well, you know,
in one speech recently,

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:19.365
I called you
suburban housewives,

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.500
and they all loved it,
but what I got, they said,

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.403
"Sir, I don't know if that's
politically correct."

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.505
I said, "Don't worry about it,
They'll get over it." Right?

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.507
-He's a political
mastermind, folks.

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:29.041
Some people still think
he's playing

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:31.210
three-dimensional chess,
but I think he's playing

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:34.113
"Chutes and Ladders,"
all-chutes addition.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.881
I hope the Trump campaign
is already printing up

00:03:35.881 --> 00:03:37.149
their new lawn signs,

00:03:37.149 --> 00:03:39.718 line:0%
"Trump 2020 --
You'll Get Over it."

00:03:39.718 --> 00:03:42.387
It's amazing, he even insults
voters he's trying to win over.

00:03:42.387 --> 00:03:43.655
He can't help himself.

00:03:43.655 --> 00:03:45.558
[ As Trump ] "And what's up
with Evangelicals?

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.727
Are these guys weird or what?

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:51.030
I mean, if Jesus is hiding
inside that little cracker,

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.698
why would they eat --
Don't eat Jesus.

00:03:52.698 --> 00:03:55.701
Don't worry. Don't worry.
They'll get over it."

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:58.204
And then Trump whined that,
because he was investigated

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:00.606
for Russian collusion,
he -- he -- should get

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:02.108
a third term.

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:04.510
-We are going to win the state
of Wisconsin,

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.446
and we are going
to win four more years.

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:09.615
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:09.615 --> 00:04:13.719
[ Crowd chanting
"Four More Years" ]

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:16.321
-And then after that, we'll go
for another four years

00:04:16.321 --> 00:04:19.558
because -- you know what,
they spied on campaign,

00:04:19.558 --> 00:04:21.927
we should get a redo
of four years.

00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:23.329
-You're still on that?

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.231
Man, when it comes
to getting over it,

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:27.399
he is no suburban housewife.

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:29.501
And even when he's pretending
to be a politician,

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:31.871
he can't shake
his loan shark DNA.

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:34.674
"The interest is 100 percent,
but let's make it 200 percent,

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:36.676
'cause I saw you lookin' at my
girlfriend, how 'bout that?"

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:39.846
The only redo anyone
is getting is us

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:43.182
listening to you bitch about
an election you won.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:46.485
But yeah, I'm sure he'll be
laid-back and cool if he loses.

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:48.154
"I may be a terrible winner,
Joe,

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:49.922
but I'm an exceptional loser.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:52.858
Congratulations,
President Biden."

00:04:52.858 --> 00:04:55.962
In fact, a day after Trump
whined about the Russia probe,

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:58.264
we got definitive evidence
that his campaign did

00:04:58.264 --> 00:05:00.866
collude with Russian
intelligence --

00:05:00.866 --> 00:05:03.836
from a Republican-led --
a Republican-led --

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.938
Senate intelligence committee.

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:07.740
-A newly released Senate report,
Natalie,

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.009
raising more red flags about
the relationship

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:13.379
between the 2016
Trump campaign and Russia.

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:15.080
According to the Senate
intelligence committee,

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.216
former campaign chairman
Paul Manafort

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:19.785
employed a Russian
intelligence officer

00:05:19.785 --> 00:05:22.054
named Konstantin Kilimnik.

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:24.157
and briefed Kilimnik
on the campaign's strategy

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:26.059
for beating Hillary Clinton.

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:28.728
The report also says Manafort
might have had a connection

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:31.297
to Russian
hack-and-leak operations.

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:34.299
-That's right, the Russian
investigation is back, baby!

00:05:34.299 --> 00:05:37.102
Remember that whole plot line
from a few seasons ago

00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:39.438
when we all got to know
and love crazy characters

00:05:39.438 --> 00:05:41.240
like Paul Manafort,
Felix Sater,

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.375
Konstantin Kilimnik,
George Papadopoulos,

00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:44.543
and Sam Clovis?

00:05:44.543 --> 00:05:46.378
You remember --
"Hogan's Zeroes."

00:05:46.378 --> 00:05:47.814
Well, they're back in the news

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:49.281
now that the Senate
Intelligence Committee

00:05:49.281 --> 00:05:51.417
has released the final volume
of its Russia report

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:53.752
with the shocking finding
that Trump campaign manager

00:05:53.752 --> 00:05:56.455
Paul Manafort shared internal
campaign polling data

00:05:56.455 --> 00:05:58.257
with a Russian
intelligence officer

00:05:58.257 --> 00:06:00.392
who may have well been involved
in the hacking.

00:06:00.392 --> 00:06:02.394
This is as definitive
as it gets.

00:06:02.394 --> 00:06:03.863
Collusion happened.

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:06.064
And the worst part is, no one
cares because it's old news.

00:06:06.064 --> 00:06:08.233
It's like finding out now
that the characters on "Lost"

00:06:08.233 --> 00:06:09.802
really did die
in the plane crash.

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:13.539
"Huh. So the island was
purgatory?

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:15.007
Okay."

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:16.709
Also, I just want to say to
the Senate and Robert Mueller

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:18.277
and everyone --
everyone else involved

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:20.880
in the Russia investigation,
way to slow walk it, fellas.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.982
You couldn't have released
definitive proof

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:26.285
of a criminal conspiracy
to cheat in the 2016 election

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:28.721
before Trump botched
a deadly pandemic

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:30.355
that left the nation in ruins?

00:06:30.355 --> 00:06:33.826
I can't wait until August 2022
when the Senate announces

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:38.064
that yes, Trump did burn all the
mail-in ballots from blue states

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:39.565
the day before the election.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.967
Trump cheated in 2016 just like
he's trying to cheat now --

00:06:41.967 --> 00:06:44.003
this time, by trying to
subvert mail-in voting

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:45.705
and sow chaos and confusion.

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:48.007
Once again, for example,
he repeated a bunch of

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:51.010
insane lies about non-existent
voter fraud.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:53.713
-If you go with this
universal mail-in,

00:06:53.713 --> 00:06:55.281
where you send millions
of votes --

00:06:55.281 --> 00:06:58.151
in California, tens of millions
of ballots being sent

00:06:58.151 --> 00:07:00.219
to everybody and their dogs.

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:02.154
Okay?
Dogs are getting them, okay?

00:07:02.154 --> 00:07:05.091
People that have been dead for
25 years are getting them.

00:07:05.091 --> 00:07:06.759
You have to see what's
happening.

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:08.760
Then you're never going to have
a fair election.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:09.895
-Right.
-I'll say this,

00:07:09.895 --> 00:07:11.531
you're never going to have
a fair election.

00:07:11.531 --> 00:07:12.965
-"And it's worse than you
think, people,

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:16.101
because one dog vote,
I don't have to tell you,

00:07:16.101 --> 00:07:19.771
counts as much as seven
human votes."

00:07:19.771 --> 00:07:21.607
Also, you're complaining about
people who have been dead

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:22.874
for 25 years getting ballots?

00:07:22.874 --> 00:07:24.476
Look, I don't like him
either,

00:07:24.476 --> 00:07:27.947
but Rudy has just as much of
a right to vote as anyone else.

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:29.715
"I vote for more soup!"

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:31.784
And does he really think dogs
are getting ballots?

00:07:31.784 --> 00:07:33.352
Like, how does he think
that works?

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:35.788
Like, you'd get an envelope
at your house

00:07:35.788 --> 00:07:37.690
from your local board of
elections addressed to Rusty,

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.258
and you'd go inside
and you say,

00:07:39.258 --> 00:07:41.293
"Rusty, Rusty,
buddy, you got some mail,"

00:07:41.293 --> 00:07:43.963
then he'd come over and just
put it in his mouth.

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:45.664
Then he would take it
into the kitchen,

00:07:45.664 --> 00:07:47.700
sit down, grab a pen,
fill it out,

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.868
stamp it with his paw,
then he would put it back

00:07:49.868 --> 00:07:51.737
in the mail, I guess,
and then it gets

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:54.173
to the country registrar,
and they take a look at it,

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:56.175
and they check Rusty's name
to, you know,

00:07:56.175 --> 00:07:57.876
the name and the registration,
and they say,

00:07:57.876 --> 00:07:59.011
"Oh, it looks good to me."

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:00.546
And then Rusty
gets on the phone

00:08:00.546 --> 00:08:02.915
and calls Joe Biden
and says "It's done,"

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:04.783
and then Joe Biden says,
"Good boy."

00:08:04.783 --> 00:08:07.553
Just as it was in 2016,
Trump's strategy in 2020

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:09.889
is not to win the most votes
but to cheat.

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:11.223
Democrats meanwhile
have been focussed

00:08:11.223 --> 00:08:12.758
on their own convention.

00:08:12.758 --> 00:08:15.127
There have been some memorable
moments, from Bernie's speech

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:17.863
in front of the National
Strategic Firewood Reserve

00:08:17.863 --> 00:08:19.665
to Michelle Obama's
powerful address,

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:22.468
to the guy from Rhode Island
apparently holding

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:24.470
a plate of calamari hostage.

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:26.505
"Give us the money or you'll
never see this plate

00:08:26.505 --> 00:08:28.807
of fried squid again."
Although I have to ask,

00:08:28.807 --> 00:08:32.377
what was the obsessive focus
on Republicans about?

00:08:32.377 --> 00:08:34.179
I mean, who cares what
Meg Whitman

00:08:34.179 --> 00:08:35.481
and John Kasich think?

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:37.315
You do know they can't
even get Republicans

00:08:37.315 --> 00:08:38.851
to listen to them, right?

00:08:38.851 --> 00:08:42.254
Kasich's speech looked like a
commercial for TD Ameritrade.

00:08:42.254 --> 00:08:44.624
"Down this path
is a path is a lifetime of debt.

00:08:44.624 --> 00:08:47.159
Down this path is
a secure retirement."

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:50.295
Outside of that, the convention
has featured inspiring stories

00:08:50.295 --> 00:08:51.897
of activists,
everyday Americans,

00:08:51.897 --> 00:08:54.567
essential workers, and some of
the party's most talented

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:56.835
rising stars, so Fox News
was desperate

00:08:56.835 --> 00:08:58.404
to counter-program it.

00:08:58.404 --> 00:09:00.839
Here's what Sean Hannity told
his viewers last night.

00:09:00.839 --> 00:09:02.941
-It was boring, it was
awkward, it was disjointed.

00:09:02.941 --> 00:09:06.278
All you got was a temper
tantrum, bumper sticker slogans

00:09:06.278 --> 00:09:08.580
about pretty much how much
they hate Donald Trump,

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:10.916
and behind the hatred of him
is a hatred

00:09:10.916 --> 00:09:14.487
of we smelly Walmart shopper
Trump supporters.

00:09:14.487 --> 00:09:16.355
-Oh, "we," Sean?

00:09:16.355 --> 00:09:19.658
So you're one of the so-called
"smelly Walmart shoppers"?

00:09:19.658 --> 00:09:21.494
When you're done with your
million-dollar

00:09:21.494 --> 00:09:22.895
cable news network gig
in Manhattan,

00:09:22.895 --> 00:09:24.730
I'm sure you're swinging by
the local Walmart to pick up

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.164
some grass seed and hair wax,

00:09:26.164 --> 00:09:28.667
maybe some Kyle Busch pajamas
for the kids, please.

00:09:28.667 --> 00:09:31.169
If your driver accidentally
went by a Walmart,

00:09:31.169 --> 00:09:33.071
you'd be screaming to him
to lock the doors.

00:09:33.071 --> 00:09:35.841
Also, no one called them that.
You called them that.

00:09:35.841 --> 00:09:37.676
If anything, you just revealed

00:09:37.676 --> 00:09:40.212
what you think
of Trump supporters.

00:09:40.212 --> 00:09:42.581
"Smelly, Walmart-shopping
Trump supporters.

00:09:42.581 --> 00:09:44.883
And I mean, Trump supporters
just stink, am I right?

00:09:44.883 --> 00:09:46.752
They're rank, probably because
they're stupid.

00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:48.520
If you gave a Trump supporter
a bar of soap,

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.522
they'd cut it in half
and put it on your toast.

00:09:50.522 --> 00:09:53.492
Ha ha!
Smelly, stupid Trump supporters.

00:09:53.492 --> 00:09:55.594
That's us, right, guys?"

